<body>
    <h1>Use Case 2.1.6.2: Admin Selects Email Template for Creates Campaign=
 Setup (Step-2)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an Admin, I want to select an email template from the available optio=
ns and preview it before finalizing the selection, so that I can ensure it =
is configured correctly for my phishing campaign.</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>This use case describes the process by which the Admin selects an email =
template for the phishing campaign. The Admin can filter templates using di=
fferent criteria such as difficulty level, geolocation, and payload type. T=
he Admin can also preview any selected email template before confirming the=
 choice for the campaign. The system ensures that templates are valid and t=
hat only the relevant templates are displayed based on the applied filters.=
</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin</strong>: Views and selects an email template, applies fil=
ters, previews the email template, and proceeds to the next campaign setup =
step.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Displays the available email templates based on=
 applied filters, shows the preview, and enables selection of the template.=
</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Admin is logged into the platform and has access to the <strong>Create N=
ew Campaign</strong> wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin has navigated to the <strong>Email Template Selection</strong>=
 step.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin has available templates loaded in the system to choose from.</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>The system supports <strong>Email Template Filtering</strong> and <stron=
g>Preview</strong> functionality.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The selected email template is confirmed for the phishing campaign.</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is enabled for the Admin=
 to proceed to the next step in the campaign creation.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Wizard: 2 Email Template</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Navigate to Email Template Selection</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin navigates to the <strong>Email Template Selection</strong> pag=
e as part of the campaign creation process.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 2: Select Email Template Language</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the <strong>Email Template Language </strong>from drop=
 down<strong>. </strong>Default language is set to <strong>English</strong>=
 (e.g., English, Spanish, Arabic, Bengali, Portuguese, French, Russian, Ind=
onesian, Hindi, Mandarin Chinese). Other language will be display in the li=
st only if E-mail template available in that language.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system filters available templates based on the chosen language.</p>=
</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 3: Select Template Type</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the <strong>Template Type</strong> from drop down<stro=
ng>. </strong>Default Template Type is set to <strong>All Templates </stron=
g>(Credential Harvesting, Financial Fraud, Malware Distribution, Data Theft=
, Account Takeover, Ransomware, Spyware, Business Email Compromise, Phishin=
g for Information, CEO Fraud). Other Template Type will be display in the l=
ist only if the Admin has added them dynamically from the setting.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 4: Search Template </strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Admin can search, and sort the available email templates:<br>
Admin can search by keywords (e.g., "Holidays Offer").<br>
Admin can sort templates by popularity (Most to Least).<br>
Admin can search for templates using keywords.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 5: Apply Phishing Email Filters</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin applies filters by clicking on the <strong>Apply Phishing Emai=
l Filters</strong> button, which opens the <strong>Apply Filters</strong> m=
odal.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the relevant filters such as <strong>Detection Difficu=
lty</strong> selected dropdown (Easy, Medium, Hard).</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the relevant filters such as <strong>Geolocation </str=
ong> selected dropdown (United States, Canada, Brazil, Bangladesh, Australi=
a, United Kingdom, Singapore, Germany, Italy, Poland, Netherlands, Belgium,=
 Mexico, Egypt, Algeria, Sudan, Saudi Arabia, Morocco, Indonesia, India, Ch=
ina)</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the relevant filters such as <strong>Payload Type</str=
ong> selected dropdown (Phishing Website, Phishing Attachment, Information =
Request, Callback Request, Phishing Link, Phishing QR Code, Social Media Ph=
ishing, Malware Payload via Embedded Media, Fake Software Updates, Fake Pay=
ment Requests, Survey/Contest Phishing, Form Grabbing, Browser Hijacking, A=
d Fraud, Account Verification Phishing).</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 6: View Available Email Templates</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin views the filtered list of available templates under <strong>A=
vailable Email Template</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Templates are displayed with their names, subjects, required employee da=
ta, and other attributes.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Use Pagination to Navigate Between Pages</p></li>
</ul>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin can view the first page of 9 <strong>Available Email Template<=
/strong>. After that it will show as pagination</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays pagination controls at the bottom of the campaign li=
st with the following options:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Previous</strong>: Navigate to the previous page.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Next</strong>: Navigate to the next page.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The page number (e.g., "1", "2", "3", etc.) is highlighted to indicate t=
he current page.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks <strong>Next</strong> or <strong>Previous</strong> to n=
avigate between pages of <strong>Available Email Template</strong>.</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>The system updates the page content and displays the <strong>Available E=
mail Template </strong>from the selected page.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 7: Preview Template</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks the <strong>Preview</strong> button next to any templat=
e they wish to review.</p></li>
<li>
<p>A preview of the selected email template is displayed, showing how it wi=
ll look to the target audience.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can review the email body, subject, and any embedded content (=
e.g., images, links).</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 8: Select Template</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>After reviewing the preview, the Admin clicks <strong>Select</strong> on=
 the desired email template.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system enables the <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button for t=
he Admin to proceed.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 9: Proceed to Next Step</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> to move to the nex=
t step in the campaign creation process.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Frontend Form Validation</strong></p>
<p><strong>Field Validation Rules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Email Template Language</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must select a language.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a valid email template la=
nguage."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Template Type</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must select a valid template type=
.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a valid template type."</=
p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Apply Phishing Email Filters</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Optional</strong>: Filters can be applied or left blank.</p></li=
>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: If applied, the filters must be valid (e.g.=
, <strong>Detection Difficulty</strong>, <strong>Geolocation</strong>, <str=
ong>Payload Type</strong>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select valid filter options."</p=
></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Email Template Selection</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Admin must select a template.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must choose at least one template=
 from the list after applying filters.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a valid email template."<=
/p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Business Rules</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"d7=
db11a5-74ab-48e3-a44e-31874618743d" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Rule</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-1</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must apply at least one filter (optional) before viewing the email=
 templates.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-2</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can preview the email templates by clicking <strong>Preview</stron=
g> next to the selected template.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-3</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must select a template before proceeding to the next step in the c=
ampaign creation.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-4</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Only valid templates are displayed after applying filters.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-5</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can only select one email template at a time.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-6</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must select a language for the email template before applying filt=
ers.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-7</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The preview functionality must display the exact rendering of the select=
ed template.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"f5=
6b6296-c340-4f2b-89ef-3e55b6621097" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Pass/Fail Condition</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-01</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select an <strong>Email Template Language</strong> and <strong=
>Template Type</strong> from the dropdown menus.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Language and type are selected and displayed correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-02</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can apply <strong>Phishing Email Filters</strong> (Detection Diffi=
culty, Geolocation, Payload Type) to filter templates.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Filters are applied successfully and affect the displayed templates.</p>=
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-03</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system displays the filtered list of available email templates based=
 on selected filters.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Only the templates that match the filters are shown.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-04</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can click <strong>Preview</strong> to view a template before selec=
ting it.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The preview of the selected template is displayed correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-05</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can close the preview window and return to the <strong>Email Templ=
ate Selection</strong> screen.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The preview window closes when clicking <strong>Close</strong>.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-06</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select a valid email template and click <strong>Select</strong=
> to choose it.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The selected template is highlighted, and the <strong>Select</strong> bu=
tton works.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-07</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can apply multiple filters (difficulty, location, payload type) an=
d the results update accordingly.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The list of templates is updated based on the selected filters.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-08</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can preview the email body of any selected template.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The preview function works and displays the email body correctly.</p></t=
d>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-09</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can proceed to the next step after selecting a template.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is enabled once a valid =
template is selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-10</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can apply <strong>Detection Difficulty</strong> filter and the lis=
t updates accordingly.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The list of templates is updated based on the selected difficulty level.=
</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-11</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can apply <strong>Geolocation</strong> filter and the list updates=
 accordingly.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The list of templates is updated based on the selected location.</p></td=
>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-12</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can apply <strong>Payload Type</strong> filter and the list update=
s accordingly.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The list of templates is updated based on the selected payload type.</p>=
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-13</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can clear the selected filters by clicking <strong>Clear</strong>.=
</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Filters are cleared and the full list of templates is displayed.</p></td=
>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-14</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can successfully search for a template using the <strong>Search</s=
trong> feature.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Search</strong> function filters templates based on the sear=
ch text.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-15</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can reset all filters using the <strong>Clear</strong> button.</p>=
</td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Clicking <strong>Clear</strong> resets all filters and shows all templat=
es.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-16</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can apply filters and search simultaneously.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Both search and filter operations work together without issues.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-17</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin is guided to the next step after selecting the email template.</p>=
</td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system proceeds to the next step in the campaign creation process af=
ter template selection.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-18</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select <strong>Simulated Phishing</strong> email templates fro=
m the list.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Only relevant <strong>Simulated Phishing</strong> templates are displaye=
d.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-19</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can filter templates based on <strong>Employee Data Required</stro=
ng> (e.g., Email Address, First Name).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The displayed templates update based on the selected employee data requi=
rements.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-20</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select a <strong>Premium</strong> template based on the subscr=
iption.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Only templates available to the user's subscription plan can be selected=
.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>System Behavior &amp; Validation</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Template Filters</strong>: Filters like <strong>Detection Diffic=
ulty</strong>, <strong>Geolocation</strong>, and <strong>Payload Type</stro=
ng> must be applied correctly to narrow down the list of available template=
s.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Template Selection</strong>: Admin can select only one template =
at a time. The system ensures that the <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong>=
 button is enabled after a valid template is selected.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Preview</strong>: Admin can preview the selected template before=
 final selection to ensure it fits the campaign requirements.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Security Handling</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Data Integrity</strong>: All email templates are securely stored=
 and only accessible to authorized Aspire Admins.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Audit Logs</strong>: All actions related to email template selec=
tion and filtering are logged for audit and troubleshooting purposes.</p></=
li>
</ul>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
